# Files whose bytes are the point.
#
# third_party/grx930 is vendored byte for byte from another repository, and its
# README records sizes and commits a re-import is checked against. Two of the
# files are data that a C program parses a line at a time. With core.autocrlf
# on, a Windows checkout rewrites every one of them to CRLF, and "byte for
# byte" is then true of the repository and false of the tree somebody builds.
#
# The golden data is the same kind of object: generated, compared exactly, and
# never edited.
#
# So: no line-ending conversion for these, on any host.
third_party/grx930/*.c          -text
third_party/grx930/*.h          -text
third_party/grx930/*.txt        -text
tests/libs/pta_gemm_golden.txt  -text
tests/libs/pta_gemm_distribution.txt  -text
